# A tempo change while playing (Transport.setTempo, INT) binds on the next bar line of the render head, which runs up
# to 100 ms and a window ahead of the sounding tick: the clock takes the new rate from that line on, never earlier,
# and the MIDI clock out follows it (a pulse every 40 ticks). The Full ensemble: 96 BPM (1.536 ticks per ms), tick 0
# 100 ms after PLAY is seen (ms 101), bar N is tick N x 3840.
tap PLAY
wait 3500
expect tick 5343
expect bpm 96
expect tick_rate 1536
# mid-bar 1: to 120 BPM from bar 2 (tick 7680)
rt tempo 120
expect bpm 96
wait 1400
expect tick 7494
expect head 7680
expect bpm 120
expect tempo_tick -1
expect tick_rate 1536
wait 200
expect tempo_tick 7680
expect tick_rate 1920
expect tick 7831
# 56 ticks before bar 3's line (11520) the head is past it already: to 60 BPM from bar 4 (tick 15360)
wait 1892
expect tick 11464
expect head 11760
rt tempo 60
wait 100
expect tick 11656
expect tick_rate 1920
wait 1950
expect tick 15380
expect tempo_tick 15360
expect tick_rate 960
expect bpm 60
expect clocks_out 385
